# Puppeteer, AI Assistant & Brave Search Rules

## Browser Automation (Puppeteer)

### Core Tools Usage
- Use `puppeteer_navigate` for all page navigation operations
  - Always include error handling and timeout settings
  - Example: `await puppeteer_navigate('https://example.com')`

- Use `puppeteer_screenshot` for visual verification
  - Store screenshots in `src/test/screenshots`
  - Include timestamp in filenames
  - Example: `await puppeteer_screenshot({ path: 'verification.png' })`

- Use `puppeteer_click` for element interactions
  - Wait for elements before clicking
  - Use specific selectors
  - Example: `await puppeteer_click('#specific-button')`

- Use `puppeteer_fill` for form interactions
  - Support both single and multiple field filling
  - Example: `await puppeteer_fill('#input', 'value')`

- Use `puppeteer_select` for dropdown interactions
  - Verify options exist before selection
  - Example: `await puppeteer_select('#dropdown', 'option')`

- Use `puppeteer_hover` for hover interactions
  - Include wait time after hover actions
  - Example: `await puppeteer_hover('.menu-item')`

- Use `puppeteer_evaluate` for client-side JavaScript execution
  - Keep evaluation functions pure
  - Example: `await puppeteer_evaluate(() => document.title)`

### General Puppeteer Rules
- Store browser session data in `src/data/sessions`
- Implement retry logic for failed operations
- Close browser instances after use
- Use TypeScript for all automation scripts

## AI Assistant Integration

- Use `generateChatCompletion` in `src/lib/aiClient.ts` for all AI calls
- Implement conversation history management in `src/lib/utils/chatHistory.ts`
- Use structured prompts from `src/data/prompts` directory
- Handle rate limiting and API errors gracefully
- Log AI interactions for debugging purposes
- Maintain context across multiple interactions

## Brave Search MCP Integration

- Store Brave Search API credentials securely in environment variables
- Use `src/lib/utils/braveSearch.ts` for all Brave Search operations
- Implement result caching to minimize API calls
- Handle pagination for search results
- Validate and sanitize search queries
- Log search operations for monitoring

## Error Handling & Testing

- Wrap all tool operations in try/catch blocks:
#tsx
try {
await puppeteer_navigate(url);
} catch (error) {
console.error(Navigation failed: ${error});
await puppeteer_screenshot({ path: 'error.png' });
}


- Run `npm run test:e2e` for end-to-end testing
- Document all automation flows in `src/docs/automation.md`
- Add error tracking and monitoring for production

## Build & Deploy

- Run `npm run build` after changes
- Add summary to `.cursor-updates` in markdown format
- Use semantic commit messages
- Test all integrations in staging environment

IMPORTANT:
- Always handle browser cleanup in try/catch blocks
- Implement proper logging for debugging
- Use TypeScript types for all operations
- Keep automation scripts modular and reusable
- Document changes to automation workflow
- Take screenshots for visual verification of critical steps